{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793444055,"nonce":"hWC3H63l8fbjgL94rMTyFLBAHM0=","title":"Recorder and headless snapshots: live recording captured nothing, and there was no tool to test components without a window","message":"The debugger is blinc_recorder. Its capture pipeline did not work end to end, and its testing module was a placeholder.\n\nFound:\n- `blinc_layout::recorder_bridge` sent its own `RecorderEventData` / `TreeSnapshotData`; the recorder's `install_hooks` downcast to `RecordedEvent` / `TreeSnapshot`. The downcast never succeeds, so a click through a live UI recorded 0 events.\n- Nothing called `capture_tree_snapshot`, so no runner produced tree snapshots.\n- `testing::HeadlessContext` had no GPU, `TestContext::click_at` only logged an event, `assert_element` did nothing.\n- `blinc_test_suite` paints through its own `GpuPaintContext` path (not the renderer a window uses), writes references into a gitignored folder and creates them on first run. 80 of 196 cases fail on this checkout. Its README documents an API that does not exist.\n- Each runner (windowed, iOS, Android, web) has its own copy of the frame loop.\n\nDone:\n- The recording data model (events, tree snapshots, primitives) moved to `blinc_core::recording`; hooks on `BlincContextState` are typed; the bridge emits the shared types; the recorder re-exports them and its hooks hold the session (any thread).\n- `blinc_recorder::testing::Headless` (feature `headless`): builds a UI with a stylesheet, runs the web runner's frame phases offscreen, drives pointer and clock, paints through the real renderer, returns `CapturedFrame`. `start_recording` / `stop_recording` / `replay` use the recorder's own session format, so a headless run opens in the debugger and a recording replays to the same frame.\n- `Golden`: PNGs in `tests/snapshots/\u003cos\u003e/`, tolerance, actual/diff images, `BLINC_SNAPSHOT=bless|off`; a platform with no goldens skips.\n- cn button goldens for every variant and state, and a mid-transition frame.\n\nOpen:\n- Call `recorder_bridge::record_frame` from the windowed, iOS, Android and web runners, and let blinc_app start a session and the debug server, so a live app feeds the debugger.\n- Keyboard and text input in `Headless` and `replay` (pointer and scroll only so far).\n- A deterministic recording clock, so a headless session's timestamps follow the manual clock.\n- Move the runners' duplicated frame loop onto one driver shared with `Headless`.\n- Retire or rebase `blinc_test_suite` (and fix its README); give the recorder's debugger preview the rendered frames, not only box snapshots.\n- Goldens for other components, and for Linux (lavapipe) and Windows.","files":null}]}